{
  "about": "Household questions and what a good answer would be. `grades` grade the fixture library's items (3 the answer, 2 useful, 1 on the subject); `pi` are patterns that must all match a real library's result for it to count (all in the title: 3; all in title and text: 2; any in the title: 1). `sets` names the sets a question is in when not only the first: \"household\" (the first 56) and \"everyday\" (the searches the everyday searches the owner tried on a Raspberry Pi (November 2026), reported apart as well). \"persona\": the questions five people asked in the persona tests of 24 November 2026 (a relative at 200% text, a parent, a stressed walker, a teenager, someone abroad), graded from the Raspberry Pi's collections. `titleNeeds`: a result whose title does not match it is graded at most 1 (a page about another medicine that mentions this one is not the answer); `not`: a result whose title matches it is graded 0 (another meaning). `nonsense`: keyboard-mashing, where nothing should be found by meaning alone. \"fish\": how to preserve fish (the owner, 28 November 2026) and four ways of doing it, graded against what the catalogue offers on them (the USDA canning guide for seafood); salting and drying have nothing in the fixture library to find.",
